# Quantum teleportation, the transmission of an unknown qubit through a shared entangled pair and two classical bits,
# modeled by the kernel in the Pauli frame. A qubit's stabilizer information is two bits: how the X (bit) operator and the
# Z (phase) operator act on it. Alice holds the unknown qubit and half of a Bell pair, Bob holds the other half. Alice
# measures her two qubits jointly, which teleports the state to Bob but with a known BYPRODUCT Pauli error determined by
# her two measurement outcomes. She sends those two classical bits to Bob, who applies the matching Pauli correction (X to
# the power of one outcome, Z to the power of the other) and recovers the exact original qubit. This file PROVES the
# protocol correct: for every measurement outcome and every qubit frame, Bob's correction exactly cancels the byproduct,
# so the recovered frame equals the input. No information is cloned, and the qubit crosses with only two classical bits.

# A classical bit, an outcome or a Pauli-frame coordinate.
form bit
  case off
  case on

# A bit flip, the X (NOT) action.
task flip
  take b, like bit
  like bit
  fork case, read b
    case off
      send back
        make on
    case on
      send back
        make off

# Apply a byproduct: flip the target when the control bit is on, leave it when off. This is the controlled bit flip that
# both the measurement byproduct and Bob's correction use, so the correction is exactly the byproduct undone.
task apply-byproduct
  take control, like bit
  take target, like bit
  like bit
  fork case, read control
    case off
      send back
        read target
    case on
      send back
        call flip
          read target

# The two classical measurement outcomes Alice sends to Bob: the bit-flip byproduct (the X correction) and the phase
# byproduct (the Z correction).
form outcome
  case sent
    link flip-bit, like bit
    link phase-bit, like bit

# The qubit in the Pauli frame: the value coordinate (the X eigenvalue) and the phase coordinate (the Z eigenvalue). These
# two bits are the full stabilizer description of the qubit being teleported.
form frame
  case qubit
    link value, like bit
    link phase, like bit

# The byproduct of the joint measurement: it flips the value by the flip outcome and the phase by the phase outcome. This
# is the Pauli error the teleported state arrives with, before Bob corrects it.
task corrupt
  take o, like outcome
  take f, like frame
  like frame
  fork case, read o
    case sent
      link flip-bit
      link phase-bit
      fork case, read f
        case qubit
          link value
          link phase
          send back
            make qubit
              bind value
                call apply-byproduct
                  read flip-bit
                  read value
              bind phase
                call apply-byproduct
                  read phase-bit
                  read phase

# Bob's correction: apply X to the power of the flip outcome and Z to the power of the phase outcome. It is the same
# controlled flips as the byproduct, so applying it after the byproduct cancels both, since a bit flip is its own inverse.
task correct
  take o, like outcome
  take f, like frame
  like frame
  fork case, read o
    case sent
      link flip-bit
      link phase-bit
      fork case, read f
        case qubit
          link value
          link phase
          send back
            make qubit
              bind value
                call apply-byproduct
                  read flip-bit
                  read value
              bind phase
                call apply-byproduct
                  read phase-bit
                  read phase

# TELEPORTATION IS CORRECT: for every measurement outcome and every qubit frame, Bob's correction cancels the byproduct
# exactly, so the recovered frame equals the input. correct o (corrupt o f) = f. The unknown qubit crosses faithfully on
# two classical bits and a shared entangled pair, proved over all four outcomes and all four input frames.
rule teleportation-recovers-the-input
  seat flip-bit, like bit
  seat phase-bit, like bit
  seat value, like bit
  seat phase, like bit
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call correct
        make sent
          bind flip-bit
            read flip-bit
          bind phase-bit
            read phase-bit
        call corrupt
          make sent
            bind flip-bit
              read flip-bit
            bind phase-bit
              read phase-bit
          make qubit
            bind value
              read value
            bind phase
              read phase
      make qubit
        bind value
          read value
        bind phase
          read phase
  fold flip-bit, phase-bit, value, phase
